1
00:00:27,527 --> 00:00:30,948
THE HUSBAND

2
00:00:35,202 --> 00:00:36,410
THIS SERIES IS FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:36,411 --> 00:00:39,039
CHILDREN WERE FILMED SAFELY
GEN AI WAS USED IN SELECT SCENES

4
00:01:05,983 --> 00:01:06,984
Are you okay?

5
00:01:08,485 --> 00:01:09,652
Yeah, I'm fine.

6
00:01:20,455 --> 00:01:21,456
We'd better hurry.

7
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:24,376
We're almost there. Come on!

8
00:01:58,535 --> 00:01:59,536
I made it.

9
00:02:00,203 --> 00:02:01,204
Come on!

10
00:02:50,712 --> 00:02:51,713
You all right?

11
00:02:52,506 --> 00:02:53,507
Yeah, I'm good!

12
00:03:14,986 --> 00:03:15,987
What do you think?

13
00:03:16,988 --> 00:03:19,241
Mmm. It's nice.

14
00:03:22,369 --> 00:03:24,079
I'm glad we came.

15
00:03:46,351 --> 00:03:48,936
So far, a damaged spinal cord

16
00:03:48,937 --> 00:03:52,816
has been deemed
almost impossible to treat.

17
00:03:53,817 --> 00:03:58,529
And Woori Together Medical Center
was the first institution in the world

18
00:03:58,530 --> 00:04:01,740
to attempt merging
3D bio-printing technology

19
00:04:01,741 --> 00:04:07,497
and stem cell therapy
to restore a damaged spinal cord.

20
00:04:08,957 --> 00:04:12,960
After three years of clinical trials

21
00:04:12,961 --> 00:04:17,923
with 32 patients
who had complete spinal cord injuries,

22
00:04:17,924 --> 00:04:22,845
approximately 80% showed
signs of sensory recovery,

23
00:04:22,846 --> 00:04:25,806
and over 60% showed

24
00:04:25,807 --> 00:04:30,687
limited but voluntary movement.

25
00:04:31,188 --> 00:04:32,938
-  Yes, keep going.
- Just one more time.

26
00:04:32,939 --> 00:04:34,608
You got to keep moving.

27
00:04:36,359 --> 00:04:38,277
That's it. Yes, well done.

28
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:41,530
Here, a patient who was
completely paralyzed for the past…

29
00:04:41,531 --> 00:04:44,409
…ten years is moving his toes.

30
00:04:45,202 --> 00:04:48,705
We have a long way to go
until they can walk again.

31
00:04:49,539 --> 00:04:53,668
However, we have seen
undeniable potential.

32
00:04:54,711 --> 00:04:57,922
And I'd like to thank Dr. Kang Taeju,

33
00:04:57,923 --> 00:05:01,927
Director of Woori Together Medical Center,
for showing us the way.

34
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:06,264
Dr. Kang, please share a few words.

35
00:05:10,352 --> 00:05:11,685
I'm sorry, Dr. Ko.

36
00:05:11,686 --> 00:05:14,814
I've been paged to the OR
for an emergency.

37
00:05:14,815 --> 00:05:16,107
Please excuse me.

38
00:05:16,733 --> 00:05:18,234
I'm sorry.

39
00:05:28,870 --> 00:05:32,331
Every second counts
for an emergency patient.

40
00:05:32,332 --> 00:05:33,917
We hope you understand.

41
00:05:35,293 --> 00:05:38,420
But while Dr. Kang is away,

42
00:05:38,421 --> 00:05:43,593
Dr. Ko will give you a more
in-depth explanation of this project.

43
00:05:44,261 --> 00:05:46,178
Please give him a big hand.

44
00:05:46,179 --> 00:05:47,930
DOUBLE-CHECK CONSENT!
SURGICAL CONSENT,

45
00:05:47,931 --> 00:05:50,725
BLOOD TRANSFUSION CONSENT,
AND PCA CONSENT

46
00:05:55,397 --> 00:05:56,398
Freer.

47
00:06:08,243 --> 00:06:10,245
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER

48
00:06:13,415 --> 00:06:15,749
…we can.

49
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:16,751
Hello.

50
00:06:21,798 --> 00:06:23,633
How are you, sir?

51
00:06:24,384 --> 00:06:25,552
Good to see you.

52
00:06:26,469 --> 00:06:27,928
I've just wrapped up the event.

53
00:06:27,929 --> 00:06:29,806
Okay. Good work.

54
00:06:30,599 --> 00:06:33,851
So, how are you feeling today?
Are you doing all right?

55
00:06:33,852 --> 00:06:37,063
Hmm. I'm not all right at all.

56
00:06:37,939 --> 00:06:40,149
Oh… Is something bothering you?

57
00:06:40,150 --> 00:06:43,485
I'm starting to see things.

58
00:06:43,486 --> 00:06:46,322
He means he's hungry.

59
00:06:46,323 --> 00:06:47,573
What?

60
00:06:47,574 --> 00:06:50,452
This fasting thing is killing me.

61
00:06:51,911 --> 00:06:53,787
Just think of it as a long nap.

62
00:06:53,788 --> 00:06:55,998
The surgery will be over in no time.

63
00:06:55,999 --> 00:06:57,207
Isn't that right, Ms. Ko?

64
00:06:57,208 --> 00:06:58,459
Of course.

65
00:06:58,460 --> 00:07:02,838
Dr. Kang is number one
in the field of spinal cord microsurgery.

66
00:07:02,839 --> 00:07:05,007
We'll begin
Chairman Kim Manseong's

67
00:07:05,008 --> 00:07:06,717
spinal stenosis surgery in 30 minutes.

68
00:07:06,718 --> 00:07:07,886
Yes, Doctor.

69
00:07:12,807 --> 00:07:15,476
-  Please, I'm begging you!
-  Calm down, ma'am!

70
00:07:15,477 --> 00:07:17,144
Please help my husband!

71
00:07:17,145 --> 00:07:18,979
- All right. Could you please wait…
- Just…

72
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:22,107
At least let a doctor see him!

73
00:07:22,108 --> 00:07:23,692
We still need you to calm down.

74
00:07:23,693 --> 00:07:24,944
What's going on over there?

75
00:07:25,779 --> 00:07:27,739
She's screaming
that her husband needs surgery.

76
00:07:28,323 --> 00:07:30,158
- Is it an emergency?
- Yeah.

77
00:07:30,742 --> 00:07:34,203
But all the surgeons on call
are in surgery right now,

78
00:07:34,204 --> 00:07:37,582
so we told her she has to wait,
but it's no use.

79
00:07:38,041 --> 00:07:41,211
She says she'll kill herself right here
and now if he can't get surgery.

80
00:07:41,670 --> 00:07:42,671
Geez.

81
00:07:46,591 --> 00:07:49,593
Please help my husband!

82
00:07:49,594 --> 00:07:50,886
Yes, we understand,

83
00:07:50,887 --> 00:07:52,930
but no one can operate on him right now.

84
00:07:52,931 --> 00:07:55,182
So please stop blocking the way
and wait outside.

85
00:07:55,183 --> 00:07:58,102
Every hospital we've been to
said the same thing!

86
00:07:59,270 --> 00:08:01,188
If he doesn't get help, he's going to die!

87
00:08:01,189 --> 00:08:04,358
This isn't going to change anything.
Hey, get them out of here.

88
00:08:04,359 --> 00:08:06,610
- No, please…
- Come on.

89
00:08:06,611 --> 00:08:09,114
- Let's go.
- Please! No!

90
00:08:09,489 --> 00:08:11,032
Sir!

91
00:08:11,783 --> 00:08:14,827
Please! Stop! Don't do this!

92
00:08:14,828 --> 00:08:15,829
Hold on.

93
00:08:18,415 --> 00:08:19,416
Dr. Kang.

94
00:08:22,252 --> 00:08:23,962
What seems to be the problem?

95
00:08:24,504 --> 00:08:29,467
His back, hips, and legs all hurt so bad
that he can't even walk properly.

96
00:08:30,051 --> 00:08:33,221
He can't go to the bathroom,
and he can't tell if he needs to go.

97
00:08:34,305 --> 00:08:36,807
Sir, we're going to try
pointing your toes up, okay?

98
00:08:36,808 --> 00:08:39,936
You can't move it, can you?

99
00:08:42,188 --> 00:08:44,231
I can't do it.

100
00:08:44,232 --> 00:08:45,442
When did this start?

101
00:08:46,234 --> 00:08:49,361
He was moving the table yesterday,
and he suddenly said his back hurt.

102
00:08:49,362 --> 00:08:50,738
He's been like this since.

103
00:08:50,739 --> 00:08:52,072
Around what time?

104
00:08:52,073 --> 00:08:54,575
It was right after breakfast, so 9 a.m.

105
00:09:01,291 --> 00:09:03,126
- Wait a minute.
- Ms. Ko.

106
00:09:03,835 --> 00:09:05,587
- What's going on?
- Well…

107
00:09:07,714 --> 00:09:09,048
Did you get the MRI yet?

108
00:09:09,049 --> 00:09:11,383
-  We should have it any minute now.
- Do we have an OR?

109
00:09:11,384 --> 00:09:15,012
OR Three. Anesthesia is almost here, too.

110
00:09:15,013 --> 00:09:16,473
Dr. Kang.

111
00:09:18,058 --> 00:09:19,433
We need to talk.

112
00:09:19,434 --> 00:09:20,601
Not now, sorry.

113
00:09:20,602 --> 00:09:23,813
You can't change the surgery schedule
for a VIP patient as you wish.

114
00:09:24,564 --> 00:09:27,609
This will put us in a tight spot.
Did you even think about that?

115
00:09:30,487 --> 00:09:31,488
I'm sorry.

116
00:09:32,072 --> 00:09:33,073
You're sorry?

117
00:09:37,619 --> 00:09:38,953
I'm sick of hearing that.

118
00:09:40,246 --> 00:09:41,956
You got anything else?

119
00:09:53,301 --> 00:09:55,095
He's got cauda equina.

120
00:09:55,845 --> 00:09:59,181
If he doesn't get surgery now,
he'll have to live with a disability.

121
00:09:59,182 --> 00:10:02,101
LEG PARALYSIS
AND BLADDER/BOWL DYSFUNCTION

122
00:10:02,102 --> 00:10:04,771
CAUSED BY COMPRESSION OF NERVES
AT THE END OF THE SPINAL CORD

123
00:10:20,537 --> 00:10:22,330
This hospital has a schedule to stick to.

124
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:26,209
You'll do Chairman Kim's surgery first.

125
00:10:26,793 --> 00:10:29,419
Chairman Kim's is a simple procedure.

126
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:32,257
This man's out of time.
He may never walk again.

127
00:10:32,715 --> 00:10:34,342
Here we go again.

128
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:38,263
There's always something more important.

129
00:10:39,264 --> 00:10:41,182
Something more urgent.

130
00:10:55,446 --> 00:10:57,157
-  Let's go.
- Yes, Doctor.

131
00:11:24,893 --> 00:11:26,852
Okay, let's verify the patient's identity.

132
00:11:26,853 --> 00:11:29,146
Park Yeongjun, 42-year-old male.

133
00:11:29,147 --> 00:11:31,440
It's an emergency decompression
for cauda equina.

134
00:11:31,441 --> 00:11:33,275
Going in for a laminectomy.

135
00:11:33,276 --> 00:11:34,776
Anesthesia, any issues?

136
00:11:34,777 --> 00:11:37,197
- All clear.
- Okay, we're going up. Blade.

137
00:11:44,787 --> 00:11:46,831
Dr. Kang. Stop this at once.

138
00:11:50,668 --> 00:11:53,962
Dr. Ko, you can't be in here.

139
00:11:53,963 --> 00:11:57,759
You know better than anyone that the OR
is a restricted zone during a procedure.

140
00:11:58,259 --> 00:11:59,969
You haven't even made an incision yet!

141
00:12:00,553 --> 00:12:03,389
Put this on hold,
and stick to the original schedule.

142
00:12:04,224 --> 00:12:07,017
This patient is critical.
It’s an emergency cauda equina case.

143
00:12:07,018 --> 00:12:10,062
Don't you hear me?
I don't give a damn what it is!

144
00:12:10,063 --> 00:12:12,649
You're putting
the entire hospital at risk!

145
00:12:13,566 --> 00:12:16,903
Do you have any idea how much Chairman Kim
has poured into this facility?

146
00:12:17,862 --> 00:12:21,115
Stop this procedure
and get Chairman Kim on the table first.

147
00:12:22,575 --> 00:12:23,576
Now!

148
00:12:26,663 --> 00:12:28,831
- Please get out.
- What?

149
00:12:29,582 --> 00:12:31,000
I said, please get out of here.

150
00:12:32,710 --> 00:12:33,711
What did you say?

151
00:12:34,796 --> 00:12:36,798
I said, get the hell out of here!

152
00:12:40,134 --> 00:12:41,135
Yes?

153
00:12:43,554 --> 00:12:44,931
Wait, what?

154
00:12:48,977 --> 00:12:51,187
Did you not hear me?
Get out of here right now!

155
00:12:55,608 --> 00:12:58,026
Please leave. Right now.

156
00:12:58,027 --> 00:13:00,280
Dr. Kang, I think you're out of line.

157
00:13:00,989 --> 00:13:02,448
This is my OR.

158
00:13:04,492 --> 00:13:05,618
Please leave.

159
00:13:08,746 --> 00:13:11,249
This is what I get
for letting you into my family.

160
00:13:44,073 --> 00:13:46,284
All right, let's resume.

161
00:13:46,784 --> 00:13:47,785
Blade.

162
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:09,182
THE HUSBAND

163
00:14:14,687 --> 00:14:16,189
SATURDAY, FEBRUARY 7
ALARM

164
00:14:58,272 --> 00:15:00,233
Do you want some coffee? I just made it.

165
00:15:11,369 --> 00:15:14,497
I had no choice yesterday.
That man was running out of time.

166
00:15:16,958 --> 00:15:18,960
Plus, Chairman Kim's surgery went well.

167
00:15:28,344 --> 00:15:31,139
All's well that ends well, huh?
Is that what you're saying?

168
00:15:32,390 --> 00:15:35,892
All right, I'm sorry
I didn't stick to the schedule.

169
00:15:35,893 --> 00:15:38,688
But it was only delayed by an hour, so…

170
00:15:39,730 --> 00:15:40,731
Only an hour?

171
00:15:41,941 --> 00:15:43,692
He's not just another VIP.

172
00:15:43,693 --> 00:15:46,319
He's the chairman
of our biggest corporate sponsor.

173
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:49,239
Seyun, it was an emergency patient.

174
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:50,658
I had no choice.

175
00:15:51,450 --> 00:15:54,661
Had we not operated on him,
he would never have walked again.

176
00:15:54,662 --> 00:15:57,874
Our hospital has
a very specific set of rules.

177
00:15:58,833 --> 00:16:00,500
And you completely ignored it.

178
00:16:00,501 --> 00:16:02,420
Are those the hospital's rules,

179
00:16:03,504 --> 00:16:05,255
or you and your dad's rules?

180
00:16:05,256 --> 00:16:06,591
What?

181
00:16:07,341 --> 00:16:08,425
Nothing.

182
00:16:08,426 --> 00:16:11,095
I'll apologize to your dad
and Chairman Kim personally.

183
00:16:11,679 --> 00:16:12,930
Yeah, you do that.

184
00:16:32,283 --> 00:16:36,162
Father, I was out of line yesterday.
I'm really sorry.

185
00:16:37,622 --> 00:16:39,624
That was really something, you know that?

186
00:16:40,291 --> 00:16:42,376
"Get out of my OR"?

187
00:16:43,377 --> 00:16:45,629
I get that we're both
technically directors here.

188
00:16:45,630 --> 00:16:47,923
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER
DIRECTOR KO DONGCHAN

189
00:16:47,924 --> 00:16:49,425
But you assume we're equals?

190
00:16:50,301 --> 00:16:51,844
Is that what you think?

191
00:16:52,595 --> 00:16:55,180
I built this hospital from the ground up,

192
00:16:55,181 --> 00:16:58,017
just to be kicked out
by my own son-in-law!

193
00:16:59,644 --> 00:17:04,147
You see, with an emergency at hand,
I wasn't thinking clearly.

194
00:17:04,148 --> 00:17:05,691
I'm really sorry.

195
00:17:10,112 --> 00:17:11,781
And the press briefing?

196
00:17:12,323 --> 00:17:15,618
Do you have any idea
what they were all saying after you left?

197
00:17:16,661 --> 00:17:20,455
Do you have any idea
how Seyun had to clean up that mess?

198
00:17:20,456 --> 00:17:25,211
And Chairman Kim was so furious
that he refused our treatment.

199
00:17:26,254 --> 00:17:28,589
So she barely managed
to convince him into…

200
00:17:33,261 --> 00:17:36,638
I promise it'll never happen again.

201
00:17:36,639 --> 00:17:37,722
I'm sorry.

202
00:17:37,723 --> 00:17:39,140
Is that right?

203
00:17:39,141 --> 00:17:41,269
It must be nice being you.

204
00:17:41,978 --> 00:17:44,020
You go around
making a mess left and right,

205
00:17:44,021 --> 00:17:46,357
and Seyun does all the cleanup.

206
00:17:50,903 --> 00:17:52,697
I'm really sorry, Father.

207
00:17:53,281 --> 00:17:55,992
Get out.
I can't even stand seeing you right now!

208
00:18:11,841 --> 00:18:14,718
Dr. Kang must've gotten
an earful from Dr. Ko.

209
00:18:14,719 --> 00:18:17,137
He looks totally deflated.

210
00:18:17,138 --> 00:18:19,097
What's with him these days?

211
00:18:19,098 --> 00:18:22,058
He never used to butt heads
with Dr. Ko like that.

212
00:18:22,059 --> 00:18:23,310
Beats me.

213
00:18:23,311 --> 00:18:25,061
It was just a matter of time.

214
00:18:25,062 --> 00:18:27,940
Knowing him,
I'd say this was bound to happen.

215
00:18:28,482 --> 00:18:31,568
Then you should've done
something beforehand, Dr. Choi.

216
00:18:31,569 --> 00:18:34,238
- Yeah, exactly.
- What was I supposed to do?

217
00:18:34,822 --> 00:18:37,033
You think he'd listen to me?

218
00:18:38,951 --> 00:18:42,370
We have to walk on eggshells
when he gets like that.

219
00:18:52,506 --> 00:18:53,507
Dr. Cha.

220
00:18:56,886 --> 00:18:58,220
Would you like some coffee?

221
00:19:00,514 --> 00:19:01,515
Maybe later.

222
00:19:15,946 --> 00:19:17,657
-  Are you going somewhere?
- Yeah.

223
00:19:18,407 --> 00:19:19,492
For an off-site meeting.

224
00:19:21,577 --> 00:19:22,578
Thank you.

225
00:19:23,579 --> 00:19:24,580
For what?

226
00:19:25,831 --> 00:19:27,500
Your dad told me.

227
00:19:28,793 --> 00:19:31,545
About the press briefing
and the situation with Chairman Kim.

228
00:19:32,546 --> 00:19:34,090
You covered for me.

229
00:19:35,299 --> 00:19:37,510
I was just doing my job
as the board director.

230
00:19:38,928 --> 00:19:44,350
Yeah, I know. It's just good to know
you might still be on my side.

231
00:19:47,228 --> 00:19:48,938
Don't think I did all that for you.

232
00:19:50,272 --> 00:19:52,649
I can't let this hospital
end up like us, can I?

233
00:20:40,489 --> 00:20:42,449
Vitals are dropping.
Give me an amp of epi.

234
00:20:42,450 --> 00:20:44,743
The patient is flatlining.
Keep compressing.

235
00:20:44,744 --> 00:20:46,703
Please, no…

236
00:20:46,704 --> 00:20:48,121
Get the crash cart in here!

237
00:21:15,483 --> 00:21:16,525
Hey, Dr. Kang…

238
00:21:33,334 --> 00:21:35,502
STAIRWELL
FIRE DOOR, KEEP CLOSED

239
00:21:35,503 --> 00:21:38,047
DO NOT PLACE OBJECTS
NEAR FIRE DOOR

240
00:21:47,348 --> 00:21:48,349
I knew you'd be here.

241
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:50,643
Hey, what's up?

242
00:21:51,477 --> 00:21:52,852
Do you want coffee?

243
00:21:52,853 --> 00:21:54,063
No, I'm fine.

244
00:21:54,772 --> 00:21:57,190
And you should lay off
the instant coffee, Doc.

245
00:21:57,191 --> 00:21:58,609
It's pure sugar, this thing.

246
00:22:00,277 --> 00:22:02,446
Got yourself a cozy little cave here, huh?

247
00:22:09,203 --> 00:22:11,163
What the… The lock still doesn't work.

248
00:22:12,289 --> 00:22:15,167
I told them this is a major security risk.

249
00:22:15,751 --> 00:22:16,836
Geez.

250
00:22:20,756 --> 00:22:22,091
You know, I was surprised.

251
00:22:23,175 --> 00:22:24,760
In the OR, I mean.

252
00:22:25,261 --> 00:22:29,598
I've known you since med school,
but I'd never seen that side of you.

253
00:22:32,184 --> 00:22:34,854
Are you doing all right?
I know it's been rough.

254
00:22:36,188 --> 00:22:39,399
Father-in-law-slash-boss, wife-slash-boss…

255
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:40,484
Which is harder?

256
00:22:41,193 --> 00:22:42,402
Both pretty hard.

257
00:22:45,531 --> 00:22:47,907
I take it things
are still not so great at home?

258
00:22:51,370 --> 00:22:54,373
How long will you keep this up for?
The tension will make you both wither.

259
00:22:55,666 --> 00:22:56,959
Tell me about it.

260
00:22:58,836 --> 00:23:00,588
Try having a real conversation.

261
00:23:02,131 --> 00:23:04,717
Okay, so how do you have this
"real conversation"?

262
00:23:05,259 --> 00:23:06,968
What do you mean how?

263
00:23:06,969 --> 00:23:09,221
You just be honest with each other.

264
00:23:11,140 --> 00:23:13,100
And what if that makes things worse?

265
00:23:13,475 --> 00:23:14,934
What do you have to lose?

266
00:23:14,935 --> 00:23:16,270
You're already at rock bottom.

267
00:23:18,314 --> 00:23:21,358
Trust me,
there are levels beneath rock bottom.

268
00:23:23,235 --> 00:23:25,069
You still have to do something.

269
00:23:25,070 --> 00:23:27,072
Because if you don't, your marriage…

270
00:23:28,198 --> 00:23:29,450
It'll really be over.

271
00:23:46,717 --> 00:23:47,718
Hey, you're home.

272
00:23:53,474 --> 00:23:55,600
I thought I'd make us dinner.

273
00:23:55,601 --> 00:23:56,769
Let's eat together.

274
00:23:59,897 --> 00:24:02,148
Remember that pajeon place
at the foot of Bukhansan?

275
00:24:02,149 --> 00:24:03,442
You used to love that place.

276
00:24:04,318 --> 00:24:06,987
You sure had a big appetite
for such a tiny girl.

277
00:24:07,696 --> 00:24:09,114
I did my best,

278
00:24:10,366 --> 00:24:11,825
but I don't know if it's as good.

279
00:24:14,620 --> 00:24:15,871
I got some makgeolli too.

280
00:24:17,081 --> 00:24:18,457
I know it's your favorite.

281
00:24:19,833 --> 00:24:21,043
Have a seat.

282
00:24:23,212 --> 00:24:26,715
Man, I don't know why makgeolli
tasted so good back then.

283
00:24:27,925 --> 00:24:29,343
I've already eaten.

284
00:24:30,511 --> 00:24:33,096
Oh. Really?

285
00:24:33,097 --> 00:24:35,975
Well, why don't
we just have a drink, then?

286
00:24:37,017 --> 00:24:38,227
I don't feel like drinking.

287
00:24:40,604 --> 00:24:42,106
Wait, Seyun.

288
00:24:43,774 --> 00:24:45,651
I made it just for you.

289
00:24:46,193 --> 00:24:47,611
Just sit with me for a while.

290
00:24:48,320 --> 00:24:49,655
I said I don't want to.

291
00:24:50,656 --> 00:24:53,909
I'm just asking you to sit with me.
Is that so hard?

292
00:25:35,617 --> 00:25:37,036
Did you change your mind?

293
00:25:42,666 --> 00:25:44,042
I'll pour you one.

294
00:25:44,043 --> 00:25:45,209
It's fine. I got it.

295
00:25:45,210 --> 00:25:47,211
I just want to do
something for you for once.

296
00:25:47,212 --> 00:25:49,214
- I said, it's fine.
- Come on, just let me…

297
00:25:54,928 --> 00:25:56,722
I said I'd do it myself!

298
00:25:58,474 --> 00:25:59,932
I told you I'd do it.

299
00:25:59,933 --> 00:26:01,310
What is wrong with…

300
00:26:11,528 --> 00:26:12,654
I'm sorry.

301
00:26:17,034 --> 00:26:19,912
But does this make you that mad?

302
00:26:20,412 --> 00:26:22,164
This is why our marriage isn't working.

303
00:26:23,540 --> 00:26:26,251
Even the smallest things turn into a mess
when we're together.

304
00:26:27,795 --> 00:26:29,254
I'll fix this up.

305
00:26:29,880 --> 00:26:31,090
It's just like our marriage.

306
00:26:32,132 --> 00:26:33,759
Shattered to pieces.

307
00:26:37,471 --> 00:26:40,641
You'll fix it? What's broken is broken.

308
00:26:41,892 --> 00:26:44,394
You can glue it together,
but it'll never be whole again.

309
00:26:44,937 --> 00:26:46,605
Are you really going to be like this?

310
00:26:46,939 --> 00:26:48,398
You always do this.

311
00:26:48,899 --> 00:26:51,150
It's always, "It's okay, we'll try again."

312
00:26:51,151 --> 00:26:52,611
As if nothing ever happened.

313
00:26:54,196 --> 00:26:56,490
What do you want from me?

314
00:26:58,117 --> 00:26:59,450
What do you want me to do?

315
00:26:59,451 --> 00:27:00,869
Tell me, I'm all ears.

316
00:27:02,079 --> 00:27:04,540
Because I honestly don't know
what more I can do.

317
00:27:05,040 --> 00:27:07,084
So just keep on living
like you always have.

318
00:27:08,085 --> 00:27:10,087
That's the only thing you know how to do.

319
00:27:19,555 --> 00:27:21,557
I'm going to fix it up, okay?

320
00:27:30,524 --> 00:27:31,942
Just throw it away.

321
00:27:36,280 --> 00:27:37,281
Seyun.

322
00:27:37,823 --> 00:27:38,824
What?

323
00:27:43,287 --> 00:27:44,329
Let's put an end to this.

324
00:27:45,205 --> 00:27:46,206
What?

325
00:27:51,086 --> 00:27:52,087
I want a divorce.

326
00:27:57,426 --> 00:27:59,052
I'm not getting divorced.

327
00:27:59,511 --> 00:28:00,596
What?

328
00:28:01,179 --> 00:28:02,763
I'm not getting divorced.

329
00:28:02,764 --> 00:28:05,934
You said no glue
can put it together, just like us.

330
00:28:06,560 --> 00:28:08,812
We're never going to be whole again.

331
00:28:09,855 --> 00:28:11,815
So why don't you want to get divorced?

332
00:28:16,528 --> 00:28:17,821
Because it's what you want.

333
00:28:21,283 --> 00:28:22,951
That's why you want to stay together?

334
00:28:23,619 --> 00:28:26,413
I don't want to give you
anything you want.

335
00:28:27,414 --> 00:28:29,791
I've made myself clear.
Let's get divorced.

336
00:28:33,003 --> 00:28:34,504
Well, try if you can.

337
00:28:35,547 --> 00:28:37,883
Guess you might get your wish
if one of us dies.

338
00:29:15,837 --> 00:29:16,963
CELEBRATING THE SUCCESS

339
00:29:16,964 --> 00:29:19,216
OF ARTIFICIAL SPINAL CORD TRANSPLANT
CLINICAL TRIAL

340
00:29:20,926 --> 00:29:23,178
What? Divorce? Are you serious?

341
00:29:25,180 --> 00:29:26,181
Yeah.

342
00:29:27,182 --> 00:29:29,393
You sure you gave this enough thought?

343
00:29:30,727 --> 00:29:33,855
Do you have any money saved up?
Are you going to start your own clinic?

344
00:29:34,940 --> 00:29:36,065
I don't know.

345
00:29:36,066 --> 00:29:37,317
How much do you have?

346
00:29:39,486 --> 00:29:41,113
Around 80 million won.

347
00:29:42,489 --> 00:29:44,408
You can't even get
an MRI scanner with that.

348
00:29:45,325 --> 00:29:47,619
Maybe a used X-ray machine at best.

349
00:29:48,328 --> 00:29:50,079
Then again, it's probably better

350
00:29:50,080 --> 00:29:52,666
than being half a director
under your father-in-law.

351
00:29:53,917 --> 00:29:55,668
Why don't you go find a salaried gig?

352
00:29:55,669 --> 00:29:57,920
You could rake in money off
physical therapy

353
00:29:57,921 --> 00:30:00,090
in a well-insured neighborhood.

354
00:30:00,966 --> 00:30:02,968
Or give people Botox
at a plastic surgery clinic.

355
00:30:08,098 --> 00:30:10,266
I need to go talk to Dr. Ha over there.

356
00:30:10,267 --> 00:30:12,352
- We'll talk later.
- All right.

357
00:30:13,020 --> 00:30:14,104
- See you.
- Yeah.

358
00:30:28,076 --> 00:30:33,123
Uh… We finally showed
the world the fruit

359
00:30:33,707 --> 00:30:36,626
of all efforts we put in
throughout the past few years.

360
00:30:38,170 --> 00:30:44,550
And I'd like to thank each and every one
of you at Woori Together Medical Clinic.

361
00:30:44,551 --> 00:30:48,055
Let us celebrate this moment with a toast.

362
00:30:53,810 --> 00:30:54,894
Cheers!

363
00:30:54,895 --> 00:30:56,480
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

364
00:31:00,817 --> 00:31:02,443
Congratulations, Dr. Kang.

365
00:31:02,444 --> 00:31:04,236
Incredible work, sir.

366
00:31:04,237 --> 00:31:05,363
Thanks.

367
00:31:06,490 --> 00:31:07,741
Hey, Taeju.

368
00:31:08,575 --> 00:31:09,618
Hey.

369
00:31:12,496 --> 00:31:13,997
Congratulations.

370
00:31:15,040 --> 00:31:16,041
Thanks.

371
00:31:18,376 --> 00:31:20,045
I know you worked really hard.

372
00:31:20,754 --> 00:31:23,215
- I'm glad it worked out.
- Yeah.

373
00:31:25,842 --> 00:31:27,135
- Talk to you later.
- Yeah.

374
00:31:34,726 --> 00:31:35,727
Congratulations.

375
00:31:37,729 --> 00:31:41,024
Your precious little project
became a huge success.

376
00:31:44,236 --> 00:31:45,278
This calls for a toast.

377
00:31:48,698 --> 00:31:49,699
What is it?

378
00:31:51,159 --> 00:31:52,828
You don't even want a toast with me?

379
00:31:57,791 --> 00:32:00,502
You don't want a toast
with a wife you want to divorce?

380
00:32:04,172 --> 00:32:05,714
What are you doing?

381
00:32:05,715 --> 00:32:07,092
This is not the place for this.

382
00:32:07,676 --> 00:32:09,386
Was it supposed to be a secret?

383
00:32:12,556 --> 00:32:13,598
I'm going to go, okay?

384
00:32:15,433 --> 00:32:16,685
Another emergency?

385
00:32:21,731 --> 00:32:22,732
Yeah.

386
00:32:23,692 --> 00:32:24,943
You should go, then.

387
00:32:26,319 --> 00:32:27,571
See you.

388
00:32:39,875 --> 00:32:40,958
SEOKGI CHUEOTANG

389
00:32:40,959 --> 00:32:43,294
- All right, here's your credit card.
-  Thank you.

390
00:32:43,295 --> 00:32:44,670
- See you again.
- Yeah.

391
00:32:44,671 --> 00:32:45,796
Taeyeong.

392
00:32:45,797 --> 00:32:48,883
Oh! What are you doing here?

393
00:32:48,884 --> 00:32:50,594
Mom, I'm here.

394
00:32:52,179 --> 00:32:53,721
Oh my, is that my baby?

395
00:32:53,722 --> 00:32:55,015
Hey, Taeju.

396
00:32:55,515 --> 00:32:57,725
Why didn't you give us a call?

397
00:32:57,726 --> 00:33:00,478
I was just passing by,
and I wanted to see you, Mom.

398
00:33:01,980 --> 00:33:04,565
Well, have you had dinner yet?

399
00:33:04,566 --> 00:33:05,816
No, not yet.

400
00:33:05,817 --> 00:33:07,776
Let me get a bowl of chueotang, Mom.

401
00:33:07,777 --> 00:33:09,862
- Wait right here, okay?
- Okay.

402
00:33:09,863 --> 00:33:12,574
You totally caught me off guard.

403
00:33:21,249 --> 00:33:23,043
Taeju, take these home.

404
00:33:25,837 --> 00:33:27,463
What's all this?

405
00:33:27,464 --> 00:33:30,507
Well, I made some spicy anchovies
and pickled cucumbers.

406
00:33:30,508 --> 00:33:33,260
And these are braised lotus roots
and black beans.

407
00:33:33,261 --> 00:33:35,055
They're all Seyun's favorites.

408
00:33:35,555 --> 00:33:37,224
Take them home and eat with her, okay?

409
00:33:37,682 --> 00:33:42,771
Oh, wow. When did you
prepare all this, Mom?

410
00:33:43,772 --> 00:33:45,648
But Mom, this is too much food.

411
00:33:45,649 --> 00:33:48,818
I mean, we still have food
you gave us last time.

412
00:33:49,277 --> 00:33:53,113
Oh, no. It's not even that much.
I just used big containers.

413
00:33:53,114 --> 00:33:57,117
Seyun must be so busy these days.
She hasn't even been able to stop by.

414
00:33:57,118 --> 00:34:00,330
Make sure she eats
home-cooked meals when she's at home.

415
00:34:03,166 --> 00:34:07,294
But honestly, Seyun and I
rarely eat at home, so it's fine.

416
00:34:07,295 --> 00:34:08,880
If you don't want it, I'm taking it.

417
00:34:09,381 --> 00:34:10,839
What's wrong with you?

418
00:34:10,840 --> 00:34:14,052
Don't take your little brother's stuff.

419
00:34:15,637 --> 00:34:16,930
Just take it, all right?

420
00:34:18,974 --> 00:34:23,144
Make sure you take good care of Seyun.

421
00:34:26,690 --> 00:34:29,317
You need some home-cooked food
to keep you going.

422
00:34:30,277 --> 00:34:31,486
Okay?

423
00:34:46,334 --> 00:34:47,335
Taeyeong.

424
00:34:48,545 --> 00:34:50,337
I'm really getting a divorce.

425
00:34:50,338 --> 00:34:51,965
Get it together.

426
00:34:52,924 --> 00:34:57,469
Mom may never say it out loud,
but you're basically her whole life.

427
00:34:57,470 --> 00:35:02,474
You used to throw a fit, saying
you could never live without your wife.

428
00:35:02,475 --> 00:35:05,437
And now you can't stand living with her?

429
00:35:06,521 --> 00:35:10,233
Look. Sometimes there are ups,
and sometimes there are downs.

430
00:35:11,151 --> 00:35:13,611
Marriage can be more volatile
than the stock market.

431
00:35:13,612 --> 00:35:15,322
That's just how it is.

432
00:35:15,864 --> 00:35:17,489
I know. I do.

433
00:35:17,490 --> 00:35:20,827
But it's not like I haven't tried
to make it work, and I don't…

434
00:35:22,537 --> 00:35:24,497
I don't know how it came to this.

435
00:35:25,332 --> 00:35:26,582
Trying isn't enough.

436
00:35:26,583 --> 00:35:30,503
You're sprinting to the left
when you should be going to the right.

437
00:35:31,046 --> 00:35:33,130
You'll just keep drifting away.

438
00:35:33,131 --> 00:35:34,257
Exactly.

439
00:35:35,717 --> 00:35:38,260
That's exactly what I'm trying to say.

440
00:35:38,261 --> 00:35:41,556
Honestly, I have no idea
what Seyun really wants.

441
00:35:45,810 --> 00:35:47,479
I'm done. I'm over it.

442
00:35:49,939 --> 00:35:52,609
I'm done trying just to be chewed out.

443
00:35:53,234 --> 00:35:54,819
I want to stop trying too.

444
00:35:56,196 --> 00:35:58,031
Let me tell you something about marriage.

445
00:35:59,032 --> 00:36:00,491
Even if you fight all the time,

446
00:36:00,492 --> 00:36:03,912
you must stick together
to find the right path.

447
00:36:21,971 --> 00:36:23,515
MONDAY, FEBRUARY 9

448
00:36:25,642 --> 00:36:28,352
Thank you for calling Olbareun,
the number one call service.

449
00:36:28,353 --> 00:36:30,021
Would you like to request a driver?

450
00:36:30,522 --> 00:36:34,901
Yeah, I'm at the Uil-dong Intersection.

451
00:36:45,203 --> 00:36:47,205
Sir, did you call for a driver?

452
00:36:49,124 --> 00:36:52,043
Yeah, I did. Please take the wheel.

453
00:37:09,769 --> 00:37:13,188
I feel like I made the call a second ago.
You got here so quickly.

454
00:37:13,189 --> 00:37:16,609
Well, I just happened to be in the area,
so I got here fast.

455
00:37:18,361 --> 00:37:19,695
Well, thank you.

456
00:37:19,696 --> 00:37:23,950
I guess today's just my lucky day.

457
00:38:25,178 --> 00:38:26,679
This isn't your room.

458
00:38:28,807 --> 00:38:29,808
Get out.

459
00:38:31,976 --> 00:38:33,853
This is my room, so get out.

460
00:38:51,663 --> 00:38:52,789
My head.

461
00:39:04,551 --> 00:39:06,260
What's with all these notifications?

462
00:39:06,261 --> 00:39:07,886
MESSAGES
MISSED CALL

463
00:39:07,887 --> 00:39:10,932
HI, I'M YOUR DESIGNATED DRIVER
PLEASE REPLY WHEN YOU SEE THIS!

464
00:39:14,143 --> 00:39:17,021
What the hell is this?

465
00:40:29,093 --> 00:40:30,553
UNKNOWN NUMBER

466
00:40:33,723 --> 00:40:35,266
UNKNOWN NUMBER
DECLINE

467
00:40:38,770 --> 00:40:40,104
UNKNOWN NUMBER

468
00:40:45,777 --> 00:40:46,778
Yes, hello?

469
00:40:48,613 --> 00:40:49,614
Hello?

470
00:40:51,199 --> 00:40:52,492
Hello?

471
00:40:54,285 --> 00:40:56,287
- What the hell?
- Mr. Kang Taeju?

472
00:40:58,498 --> 00:40:59,999
Yes, speaking. Who's this?

473
00:41:00,625 --> 00:41:03,002
I'm the driver
who drove you to your house.

474
00:41:03,795 --> 00:41:04,837
Oh, yeah. Last night?

475
00:41:05,380 --> 00:41:07,172
Well, early this morning, sir.

476
00:41:07,173 --> 00:41:10,217
Oh, yes. So what's this about?

477
00:41:10,218 --> 00:41:13,845
I just wanted to ask
when you could pay me.

478
00:41:13,846 --> 00:41:16,766
Did I not pay you for the service?

479
00:41:17,976 --> 00:41:19,059
Sorry about that.

480
00:41:19,060 --> 00:41:21,812
If you could text me
your bank account number,

481
00:41:21,813 --> 00:41:24,356
I'll wire it to you right away.

482
00:41:24,357 --> 00:41:28,735
Actually, I'm not
talking about that money.

483
00:41:28,736 --> 00:41:29,820
I beg your pardon?

484
00:41:29,821 --> 00:41:32,281
- Your wife.
- My wife?

485
00:41:33,032 --> 00:41:35,033
Remember the job you asked me to do?

486
00:41:35,034 --> 00:41:37,036
I asked you to do something?

487
00:41:37,453 --> 00:41:38,538
Do you not remember?

488
00:41:39,163 --> 00:41:41,290
No, I don't remember
anything of that sort.

489
00:41:41,791 --> 00:41:44,544
Why is this prick playing dumb?

490
00:41:46,462 --> 00:41:47,797
What did you just call me?

491
00:41:48,631 --> 00:41:49,881
"Prick"?

492
00:41:49,882 --> 00:41:50,966
Listen.

493
00:41:50,967 --> 00:41:52,801
You better watch your mouth.

494
00:41:52,802 --> 00:41:55,054
- I said listen.
- You listen.

495
00:41:55,471 --> 00:41:57,806
If you don't apologize now,
I'm calling the cops.

496
00:41:57,807 --> 00:41:59,350
Mr. Kang Taeju!

497
00:41:59,934 --> 00:42:02,395
Don't be like this all of a sudden.

498
00:42:02,937 --> 00:42:04,688
You're making me real sad.

499
00:42:04,689 --> 00:42:09,484
I thought we were on the same page,
but if you keep playing dumb--

500
00:42:09,485 --> 00:42:12,612
- Okay, I'm hanging up.
- It's making me so sad.

501
00:42:12,613 --> 00:42:14,490
What is this nutjob…

502
00:42:26,627 --> 00:42:28,463
Hey, Dr. Kang! Hey!

503
00:42:30,923 --> 00:42:32,425
What happened to your wife?

504
00:42:33,259 --> 00:42:34,384
What do you mean?

505
00:42:34,385 --> 00:42:35,970
She didn't show up to golf today.

506
00:42:37,764 --> 00:42:39,348
Seyun stood people up?

507
00:42:40,099 --> 00:42:42,518
God, do you know
what a tight spot she put me in?

508
00:42:43,519 --> 00:42:46,271
She begged me to set up the round
with the association president,

509
00:42:46,272 --> 00:42:47,982
and she flaked on me without a word.

510
00:42:48,357 --> 00:42:49,650
Just unbelievable…

511
00:42:50,860 --> 00:42:53,820
Your wife.
Remember the job you asked me to do?

512
00:42:53,821 --> 00:42:56,074
Why is this prick playing dumb?

513
00:42:56,699 --> 00:42:59,367
Chiung. Let's talk later, okay?

514
00:42:59,368 --> 00:43:00,453
Okay.

515
00:43:08,628 --> 00:43:11,631
Hey, what's going on?
Why did you stand up Chiung?

516
00:43:12,882 --> 00:43:14,175
Mr. Kang.

517
00:43:15,635 --> 00:43:18,513
How could you hang up on me like that?
I was talking.

518
00:43:19,680 --> 00:43:20,807
Who's this?

519
00:43:21,599 --> 00:43:24,060
It's me, the driver from earlier.

520
00:43:26,729 --> 00:43:27,730
I see.

521
00:43:28,689 --> 00:43:31,317
So why do you have my wife's phone?

522
00:43:33,694 --> 00:43:35,488
I can't believe you.

523
00:43:38,074 --> 00:43:40,201
What… What the hell do you want?

524
00:43:41,536 --> 00:43:43,954
Where's my wife? Put her on the phone.

525
00:43:43,955 --> 00:43:45,373
You're making me so sad…

526
00:43:46,541 --> 00:43:47,834
I think I'm going to tear up.

527
00:43:48,334 --> 00:43:50,293
Put my wife on the phone right now!

528
00:43:55,633 --> 00:43:57,760
UNKNOWN NUMBER

529
00:44:02,056 --> 00:44:03,933
Anyway, that being said…

530
00:44:07,395 --> 00:44:09,563
I want you to get rid of my wife.

531
00:44:09,564 --> 00:44:10,647
What did you say?

532
00:44:10,648 --> 00:44:12,315
I'll pay you, okay?

533
00:44:12,316 --> 00:44:14,317
I'll pay you 300… No.

534
00:44:14,318 --> 00:44:17,320
I'll pay you 500 million won, so please.

535
00:44:17,321 --> 00:44:21,658
So you want me to get rid of your wife?

536
00:44:21,659 --> 00:44:22,660
Yeah.

537
00:44:26,956 --> 00:44:29,791
UNKNOWN NUMBER

538
00:44:34,839 --> 00:44:36,883
Did you see the picture and the video?

539
00:44:37,508 --> 00:44:39,635
Yes, I did.

540
00:44:42,638 --> 00:44:44,974
But my wife…

541
00:44:45,683 --> 00:44:46,684
You didn't…

542
00:44:48,644 --> 00:44:50,396
It's not what I think, right?

543
00:44:50,980 --> 00:44:52,647
Unfortunately…

544
00:44:52,648 --> 00:44:53,941
Your wife is

545
00:44:55,067 --> 00:44:56,360
still alive.

546
00:44:58,446 --> 00:45:03,241
But I'll take care of her
as soon as you send me the money,

547
00:45:03,242 --> 00:45:04,451
so don't worry about it.

548
00:45:04,452 --> 00:45:06,954
Hold on a minute, sir. It's just…

549
00:45:07,997 --> 00:45:10,624
Why are you doing this to us?

550
00:45:10,625 --> 00:45:13,126
I could ask you the same thing!

551
00:45:13,127 --> 00:45:14,628
Why are you doing this?

552
00:45:14,629 --> 00:45:17,423
You can't put me up to something
and pretend you don't remember!

553
00:45:18,883 --> 00:45:20,760
Look, I never put you up to…

554
00:45:23,262 --> 00:45:26,223
I don't know
what you're talking about, okay?

555
00:45:26,224 --> 00:45:28,600
You're only making things
more difficult, boss.

556
00:45:28,601 --> 00:45:31,353
And this video. Is that even me?

557
00:45:31,354 --> 00:45:33,188
This has to be fake.

558
00:45:33,189 --> 00:45:34,523
Is that what you think?

559
00:45:42,573 --> 00:45:43,907
No, I mean…

560
00:45:43,908 --> 00:45:46,285
Listen, I may have said
some things I didn't mean

561
00:45:46,869 --> 00:45:48,912
because I was drunk,

562
00:45:48,913 --> 00:45:52,457
but you shouldn't have taken it seriously.

563
00:45:52,458 --> 00:45:53,459
And?

564
00:45:54,502 --> 00:45:57,128
Please let my wife go. I'm begging you.

565
00:45:57,129 --> 00:45:58,213
Sir.

566
00:45:58,214 --> 00:46:02,008
First, you want me to kill her,
and now you want me to let her live?

567
00:46:02,009 --> 00:46:03,593
Yes, please don't kill her.

568
00:46:03,594 --> 00:46:07,847
If you just let her go,
I won't tell a soul about what happened.

569
00:46:07,848 --> 00:46:09,849
Here's the thing, boss.

570
00:46:09,850 --> 00:46:13,396
I hate it when people
make things complicated.

571
00:46:13,813 --> 00:46:17,649
People who don't keep their promises?
I just can't stand them.

572
00:46:17,650 --> 00:46:21,654
I'm going to ask you one last time,
so really think before you answer.

573
00:46:23,281 --> 00:46:26,950
Do you want your wife dead or alive?

574
00:46:26,951 --> 00:46:30,620
I want her to live. Let her live. Please.

575
00:46:30,621 --> 00:46:31,705
All right, then.

576
00:46:31,706 --> 00:46:34,791
I'll let it slide this time…

577
00:46:34,792 --> 00:46:36,584
…but don't let this happen again.

578
00:46:36,585 --> 00:46:41,131
Yes, of course.
Thank you so much. Thank you.

579
00:46:41,132 --> 00:46:44,134
But you know
there'll be extra charges, right?

580
00:46:44,135 --> 00:46:45,928
You changed the options.

581
00:46:46,804 --> 00:46:47,971
What options?

582
00:46:47,972 --> 00:46:52,226
It's 500 million to kill your wife,
and 1 billion won to let her live.

583
00:46:52,935 --> 00:46:54,602
You have three hours.

584
00:46:54,603 --> 00:46:55,687
What?

585
00:46:55,688 --> 00:46:59,858
If I don't get my one billion won
in three hours, consider your wife dead.

586
00:46:59,859 --> 00:47:04,070
And if you go to the cops
or ignore my calls, she's dead.

587
00:47:04,071 --> 00:47:05,488
Hold on, three hours is too--

588
00:47:05,489 --> 00:47:07,907
Now, you won't be able
to reach your wife's phone.

589
00:47:07,908 --> 00:47:12,787
It's 10:25 a.m. right now,
and I'll be in touch in three hours.

590
00:47:12,788 --> 00:47:13,998
And, boss?

591
00:47:14,582 --> 00:47:16,374
Don't disappoint me anymore.

592
00:47:16,375 --> 00:47:20,463
Hello?

593
00:47:27,595 --> 00:47:28,845
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER

594
00:47:28,846 --> 00:47:30,890
I want you to get rid of my wife.

595
00:47:31,932 --> 00:47:33,517
I'll pay you, okay?

596
00:47:33,934 --> 00:47:36,603
I'll pay you 300… No.

597
00:47:36,604 --> 00:47:38,522
I'll pay you 500 million won, so please.

598
00:47:40,274 --> 00:47:44,779
So you want me to get rid of your wife?

599
00:47:47,281 --> 00:47:48,324
Yeah.

600
00:47:50,993 --> 00:47:53,703
Thank you for calling Olbareun,
the number one call service.

601
00:47:53,704 --> 00:47:57,415
Yeah, I'm at the Uil-dong Intersection.

602
00:47:59,877 --> 00:48:03,422
Yeah, I did. Please take the wheel.

603
00:48:07,385 --> 00:48:09,762
I definitely saw his face.

604
00:48:11,389 --> 00:48:13,557
But I don't remember it.

605
00:48:46,632 --> 00:48:47,799
CALLING

606
00:48:54,265 --> 00:48:56,516
-  Hello?
- Hello?

607
00:48:56,517 --> 00:49:02,313
Is this the driver
who drove me home last night?

608
00:49:02,314 --> 00:49:03,523
Oh, Uil-dong Intersection?

609
00:49:03,524 --> 00:49:05,358
Why didn't you answer your phone?

610
00:49:05,359 --> 00:49:06,860
Nobody was there when I got there.

611
00:49:14,076 --> 00:49:16,786
Thank you for calling Olbareun,
the number one call service.

612
00:49:16,787 --> 00:49:18,413
Would you like to request a driver?

613
00:49:18,414 --> 00:49:22,667
Hi. I'm looking for the driver
who drove me home last night.

614
00:49:22,668 --> 00:49:25,503
And you called from this number, correct?

615
00:49:25,504 --> 00:49:27,590
- Yeah.
- Just a moment.

616
00:49:28,716 --> 00:49:32,218
It seems like this request was canceled
because the driver couldn't reach you.

617
00:49:32,219 --> 00:49:35,305
No. I definitely used
your service last night.

618
00:49:35,306 --> 00:49:37,265
According to our records,

619
00:49:37,266 --> 00:49:40,435
your designated driver called you
three times at 1:47 a.m. this morning

620
00:49:40,436 --> 00:49:44,564
but gave up and accepted another customer.

621
00:49:44,565 --> 00:49:46,984
What? I didn't pick up?

622
00:49:47,443 --> 00:49:49,611
It looks like you called
for another driver too.

623
00:49:49,612 --> 00:49:51,529
Please contact the other service provider.

624
00:49:51,530 --> 00:49:53,157
I… Wait.

625
00:50:47,127 --> 00:50:49,505
SEONGJIN POLICE STATION

626
00:51:03,686 --> 00:51:05,436
INCOMING VIDEO CALL
UNKNOWN NUMBER

627
00:51:09,066 --> 00:51:10,609
Seyun.

628
00:51:11,569 --> 00:51:16,698
What are you… What the hell are you doing?

629
00:51:16,699 --> 00:51:17,825
Honey.

630
00:51:18,784 --> 00:51:20,911
No! Stop it! No!

631
00:51:21,537 --> 00:51:23,329
Sir, what are you doing?

632
00:51:23,330 --> 00:51:25,915
Please! Please don't do that!

633
00:51:25,916 --> 00:51:28,251
Please pull her up! Please, sir!

634
00:51:30,296 --> 00:51:31,297
Seyun…

635
00:51:34,091 --> 00:51:35,508
Are you out of your mind?

636
00:51:35,509 --> 00:51:36,927
What the hell are you doing?

637
00:51:38,387 --> 00:51:42,223
You're the one who broke the deal
and tried to go to the cops.

638
00:51:42,224 --> 00:51:43,642
Did you think I wouldn't know?

639
00:51:48,939 --> 00:51:51,025
Why do you keep
disappointing me like this?

640
00:51:56,822 --> 00:51:58,449
I'm sorry, sir.

641
00:51:59,575 --> 00:52:02,077
You should be thanking me right now.

642
00:52:03,203 --> 00:52:08,249
Your wife could have died,
and I stopped that.

643
00:52:08,250 --> 00:52:09,500
Right.

644
00:52:09,501 --> 00:52:13,297
There's only so much
a person can tolerate.

645
00:52:13,922 --> 00:52:16,383
And I've reached my limit.

646
00:52:20,220 --> 00:52:21,347
I'm very sorry, sir.

647
00:52:22,973 --> 00:52:26,017
It looks like I gave you too much time.

648
00:52:26,018 --> 00:52:30,021
Let me fix that so you don't get
any more stupid ideas.

649
00:52:30,022 --> 00:52:31,105
What?

650
00:52:31,106 --> 00:52:34,109
You have one hour to get my one billion.

651
00:52:34,610 --> 00:52:37,488
Sir, one hour is far too short.

652
00:52:38,030 --> 00:52:39,406
I said what I said.

653
00:52:39,948 --> 00:52:41,032
CALL ENDED

654
00:52:41,033 --> 00:52:42,910
Hello? Hello…

655
00:53:13,273 --> 00:53:14,691
CALLING
FATHER-IN-LAW

656
00:53:14,692 --> 00:53:17,235
The number you dialed is not available…

657
00:53:17,236 --> 00:53:18,404
HOSPITAL FRONT DESK

658
00:53:19,738 --> 00:53:21,823
Woori Together Medical Center.
How may I help you?

659
00:53:21,824 --> 00:53:23,242
Hi, it's Kang Taeju here.

660
00:53:23,659 --> 00:53:25,743
Is Dr. Ko at the hospital right now?

661
00:53:25,744 --> 00:53:29,748
Dr. Ko is currently in surgery.

662
00:53:35,295 --> 00:53:37,088
The number you dialed is not available…

663
00:53:37,089 --> 00:53:38,090
CALLING
MOTHER-IN-LAW

664
00:53:45,597 --> 00:53:48,142
MODU BANK

665
00:53:55,274 --> 00:53:57,651
- Dr. Kang, long time no see.
- Hi.

666
00:53:58,527 --> 00:53:59,987
So, how have you been?

667
00:54:00,863 --> 00:54:04,699
Actually, I need
to take out a loan urgently.

668
00:54:04,700 --> 00:54:05,701
Okay.

669
00:54:06,118 --> 00:54:08,370
How much are you looking to take out?

670
00:54:08,746 --> 00:54:11,372
Well, I'd like to withdraw
all 80 million from my account,

671
00:54:11,373 --> 00:54:13,584
and I need an additional 920 million.

672
00:54:14,334 --> 00:54:15,626
Did you say 920 million won?

673
00:54:15,627 --> 00:54:17,212
Yeah, and…

674
00:54:18,422 --> 00:54:20,631
Could I get it within 50 minutes?

675
00:54:20,632 --> 00:54:24,385
I'm sorry, but even for our VIP clients,

676
00:54:24,386 --> 00:54:28,014
it'll take at least two weeks
for the papers to be approved.

677
00:54:28,015 --> 00:54:32,895
You probably couldn't even take out
a private loan that big on the same day.

678
00:54:50,913 --> 00:54:52,789
RECENT CALLS

679
00:55:08,347 --> 00:55:11,599
STOP BEFORE CROSSING

680
00:55:11,600 --> 00:55:12,808
STOP

681
00:55:12,809 --> 00:55:13,976
TRAIN APPROACHING

682
00:55:13,977 --> 00:55:15,521
TRAIN PASSING
STOP

683
00:55:48,470 --> 00:55:51,181
INCOMING VIDEO CALL
UNKNOWN NUMBER

684
00:55:59,815 --> 00:56:00,899
Hello?

685
00:56:01,608 --> 00:56:02,733
Hey, boss.

686
00:56:02,734 --> 00:56:04,403
It's almost time.

687
00:56:08,574 --> 00:56:10,199
Is my wife okay?

688
00:56:10,200 --> 00:56:12,118
She's fine for now.

689
00:56:12,119 --> 00:56:13,704
And my one billion won?

690
00:56:15,205 --> 00:56:17,832
Yeah. I have it.

691
00:56:17,833 --> 00:56:19,751
Let me see it.

692
00:56:23,213 --> 00:56:24,715
Each contains 500 million.

693
00:56:26,133 --> 00:56:27,550
One billion in total.

694
00:56:27,551 --> 00:56:30,344
I wouldn't expect any less
from a director at a hospital.

695
00:56:30,345 --> 00:56:35,308
I mean, honestly, most people could
never even see a billion won in cash.

696
00:56:35,309 --> 00:56:36,892
Where do I take it?

697
00:56:36,893 --> 00:56:38,979
I forgot to tell you that.

698
00:56:39,730 --> 00:56:43,025
Come to 43-87, Sajiro-gil.

699
00:56:43,442 --> 00:56:46,862
Be here within 30 minutes,
and you have to come alone.

700
00:56:47,279 --> 00:56:49,781
You know that's the only way
to save your wife, right?

701
00:56:50,282 --> 00:56:51,575
I'll be waiting.

702
00:56:58,707 --> 00:57:00,792
Up ahead, turn right.

703
00:57:04,379 --> 00:57:06,922
Entering school zone.
Please drive carefully.

704
00:57:06,923 --> 00:57:09,468
SCHOOL ZONE

705
00:57:12,929 --> 00:57:14,973
In 400 meters, keep straight.

706
00:57:22,230 --> 00:57:24,274
Turn left.

707
00:57:31,990 --> 00:57:34,368
In 300 meters, keep straight.

708
00:57:39,039 --> 00:57:40,582
Up ahead, turn right.

709
00:57:45,337 --> 00:57:48,757
Take the slight left into the alley.
Then, turn left.

710
00:57:51,134 --> 00:57:53,553
Continue straight to 43, Sajiro-gil.

711
00:57:54,346 --> 00:57:56,264
Please drive safely.

712
00:58:00,060 --> 00:58:01,853
Up ahead, turn left.

713
00:58:26,211 --> 00:58:27,963
Hey, are you okay?

714
00:58:29,464 --> 00:58:32,300
Hey! Can you hear me?

715
00:58:36,555 --> 00:58:37,723
Let me call an ambulance.

716
00:58:38,432 --> 00:58:39,558
Just hang in there.

717
00:58:41,476 --> 00:58:42,769
Hey, my…

718
00:58:43,270 --> 00:58:45,564
Yes?

719
00:58:46,398 --> 00:58:48,191
My one billion won…

720
00:58:49,860 --> 00:58:50,861
What was that?

721
00:58:51,236 --> 00:58:53,363
Did you bring my billion won?

722
00:58:53,989 --> 00:58:57,033
What? I can't hear you.
Can you speak up a little?

723
00:58:58,493 --> 00:59:00,203
I said, did you bring my billion won?

724
00:59:09,379 --> 00:59:14,301
THE HUSBAND

725
00:59:54,424 --> 00:59:56,091
You know where Ms. Ko is, don't you?

726
00:59:56,092 --> 00:59:57,760
I'm going to your wife now.

727
00:59:57,761 --> 01:00:00,222
There's no time to be screwing around!

728
01:00:00,889 --> 01:00:02,640
This guy is a psycho!

729
01:00:02,641 --> 01:00:04,183
My wife's in danger!

730
01:00:04,184 --> 01:00:06,936
Let me out of here!

731
01:00:06,937 --> 01:00:08,729
Who are you? What do you want?

732
01:00:08,730 --> 01:00:11,357
If you disappoint me
with another dumb stunt,

733
01:00:11,358 --> 01:00:13,901
you will pay for it dearly.

734
01:00:13,902 --> 01:00:16,529
I can actually get you the money you want.
I promise. I swear.

735
01:00:16,530 --> 01:00:18,948
You can have this
on top of the original two billion.

736
01:00:18,949 --> 01:00:20,574
-  Just because you're rich…
- Honey!

737
01:00:20,575 --> 01:00:21,868
You think you can mock me?

738
01:00:23,829 --> 01:00:26,413
What happened to your wife is all on you.

739
01:00:26,414 --> 01:00:28,416
Translated by Hyun Sik Yoon

